Takes out: nothing -- a probe: ioapic_race says "NOT ASKED -- alone" at four processors as well, as it would were the other three never to come. Since #779 the ioapic judge takes those words for NOT ASKED on one processor, and only there: at four its verdict must stay WRONG.
Accel: tcg
Script: scripts/merge-test-x86_64.sh
Script: -a
Script: kvm
Script: -e
Script: 23
Script: -G
Expect: merge-test: entry 23 kvm -smp 4 -- WRONG \(ioapic\)
Note: at the merge test's own -smp 4. Accel: tcg because under KVM ablate.sh would give the script --kvm, which it does not take; the run's own -a kvm names the accelerator. One accelerator, as every other patch run through the merge test: its exit status is its count of WRONG lines, and ablate.sh reads 2 and 3 as a run not made, so a line caught under both accelerators read as a run that did not start.

